 "new_string": "do not overgeneralize. This is instance-specific geometric evidence; infer the support from the current exemplar in every recurrence.\n\n### Fresh recurrence: task-fef9acc6, connect aligned diamond motifs\n\nOne demo and an accepted fresh test support a line-connector rule for repeated color-2 diamond motifs. Identify each diamond as four cardinal cells around its center (top, bottom, left, right), with a one-cell diagonal-background gap in its 3×3 footprint. Whenever two such diamonds are aligned horizontally or vertically, connect their facing cardinal 2-cells through the intervening gap using color 1; preserve the diamonds and all other cells. In demo 1 (10×15), diamonds centered at (1,3), (1,10), and (5,10) were present. The output filled row 1, columns 5–8 between the first two, and row 3, column 10 between the vertically aligned right pair. In the accepted 9×15 test, diamonds were centered at (2,2), (6,2), (4,7), and (6,10); the output filled (4,2) between the vertically aligned left pair and row 6, columns 4–8 between the horizontally aligned lower pair. No diagonal connector was made between the other centers. This is direct but limited evidence: apply only to recognizable cardinal diamond motifs and aligned pairs, not arbitrary objects or diagonal pairs. One initial attempted grid was malformed (a row had 14 cells instead of 15), so mechanically check every row width before serializing."
